course: dictionary
lesson: 1915
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «Noah had practised fighting-game combos for weeks.» Here a combo is a quick series of moves in a game, done one after another to score extra points.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in a food shop. A meal combo is a set of things that go together, like a burger, chips and a drink. So before you decide, ask: is this text about games, food, music or a lock?
explain: Combo is an informal word, so you will hear it in chat, games and adverts more than in a formal essay. Check the clues around it, then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Combo is short for combination.
fact: A combo can be a set of things that go together, like a meal deal of burger, chips and drink.
fact: In games, a combo is a series of quick moves or hits done one after another for extra points.
fact: A jazz combo is a small band of musicians, often playing jazz.
fact: Combo is informal, so keep it for chatting, not for formal writing.
exercise: «Noah had practised fighting-game combos for weeks.» In this sentence, what is a combo? | The code on a lock | *A series of quick moves that scores extra points | A lunch deal with burger and chips | A small band of musicians
exercise: Lena says, "I'll have the meal combo, please." What does combo mean here? | A quick move in a game | *A set of things that go together, like a burger, chips and a drink | A jazz band playing late at night | A number to open a lock
exercise: Which group is a jazz combo? | *A small group of musicians playing together | A bag of sweets for the bus | A video game with lots of levels | A menu with burgers only
test: «Ollie demonstrated a combo on the sofa and his little sister got an elbow in the eye.» What does combo mean here? | A soft cushion for the sofa | A cup of hot chocolate | *A quick series of moves, one after another | A quiet, slow song
test: In the phrase «a winning combo», what does combo most likely mean? | A sad song | A lost shoe | *A winning combination of things that work well together | A cake made with two kinds of fruit
exam: Which phrase means a meal deal with burger, chips and a drink? | A combo move in a game | A jazz combo | The combo of a lock | *A meal combo
